     "type": "example",
     "title": "When the Cycle Breaks: A Real-World Revenue Disaster",
     "content": "**Mercy General Hospital** (a composite based on real industry cases) averaged **18% initial denial rates** — well above the industry benchmark of 5-10%. Investigation revealed the root causes:\n\n• **Registration errors**: 12% of accounts had wrong insurance IDs because front-desk staff were copying from expired cards\n• **Missing authorizations**: Surgical cases proceeded without prior auth 8% of the time — each denial averaged **$15,000** in lost revenue\n• **Coding lag**: Coders were 14 days behind, causing late charge submissions that violated payer timely filing limits (typically **90-365 days** depending on the payer)\n• **No CDI program**: Physicians documented 'pneumonia' without specifying organism or severity, losing the hospital an average of **$4,200 per DRG** in undercoding\n\nThe cumulative impact: **$34 million in preventable revenue loss** annually. After implementing an integrated RCM improvement program — real-time eligibility checks, embedded CDI specialists, automated charge reconciliation — their denial rate dropped to **6%** within 18 months and they recovered **$22 million** in the first year.",
