     "explanation": "RCM is the complete administrative and clinical process for tracking patient care episodes from registration through final payment collection. Medical billing — submitting claims to payers — is just one step within that larger cycle. AHIMA defines RCM as all functions that contribute to capturing, managing, and collecting patient service revenue, encompassing front-end (registration, verification), mid-cycle (coding, charge capture), and back-end (claims, denials, A/R) processes.",
