     "explanation": "The **CRCR (Certified Revenue Cycle Representative)** from HFMA is designed as the foundational RCM credential, covering patient access, billing, collections, compliance, and financial counseling. The CHFP is a higher-level strategic finance credential. CCS is AHIMA's coding certification, not RCM-focused. CRCE-I is from AAHAM and targets experienced institutional billing professionals, not entry-level RCM roles.",
