     "explanation": "**Phase 2: Clinical Documentation & Coding** (Lessons 4-7) is where CDI programs ensure documentation supports medical necessity and accurate code assignment. While Phase 1 handles financial clearance and Phase 3 handles claim submission, it is Phase 2 where the clinical-financial translation occurs. Phase 5 (compliance and analytics) monitors quality but does not create the documentation. The strength of the entire downstream revenue cycle depends on the quality of Phase 2.",
